sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-05> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch09-05--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch09-05--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch09-05: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.79" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.785"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The rule, the closed finite setting, and the alternatives (monotonic randomization, or simple repetition as in rules 0R and 90R) are fully specified, and Wolfram already records a concrete period for one run. Re-simulation with a fixed disorder statistic can confirm or refute the non-monotonic, non-ergodic behavior at practical sizes. The thermodynamic-limit reading of the Second Law is the main residual interpretation, not a missing dataset." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Simulate second-order rule 37R on finite rings from many initial conditions and track a disorder measure, the recurrence time, and the fraction of the state space visited. The claim is confirmed if disorder fluctuates without a systematic rise and orbits stay non-ergodic and non-trivially long; it is refuted if disorder rises monotonically to equilibrium or the evolution is the short-period repetitive type." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Any finite reversible system eventually recurs, so 'indefinitely' has to be read relative to the recurrence time.", "A cellular-automaton disorder measure is only a proxy for thermodynamic entropy." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch09-05--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch09-05--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch09-05--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch09-05 by Grok 4.7: 0.74" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.74"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch09-05--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-05> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch09-05--grok--operationalizability> .
